🛠️ 2. Arrays Class

The `Arrays` class is part of:

```java id="a1"
import java.util.Arrays;
```

It provides utility methods for common array operations.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Common Methods

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 sort()

Sorts an array in ascending order.

```java id="a2"
int[] nums = {5, 2, 9, 1};
Arrays.sort(nums);
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(nums));
```

Output:

```text id="a3"
[1, 2, 5, 9]
```

---

🔹 toString()

Converts array to readable string.

```java id="a4"
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(nums));
```

---

🔹 equals()

Compares two arrays.

```java id="a5"
int[] a = {1, 2, 3};
int[] b = {1, 2, 3};

System.out.println(Arrays.equals(a, b));
```

Output:

```text id="a6"
true
```

---

🔹 fill()

Fills all elements with a value.

```java id="a7"
int[] arr = new int[5];
Arrays.fill(arr, 7);
```

---

🔹 binarySearch()

Searches sorted array.

```java id="a8"
int index = Arrays.binarySearch(nums, 5);
```

---

📌 Complete Example

```java id="a9"
import java.util.Arrays;

class ArraysClassDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] numbers = {4, 1, 3, 2};

        Arrays.sort(numbers);

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(numbers));
        System.out.println(Arrays.binarySearch(numbers, 3));
    }
}
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Important Notes

✔ `binarySearch()` works correctly only on sorted arrays.
✔ `toString()` is useful for debugging.
✔ `equals()` compares contents, not references.

---

🎯 Why Learn Arrays Class?

✔ Reduces manual coding
✔ Improves productivity
✔ Frequently used in coding interviews

